---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About Les Xu" description="About Les Xu, Vietnam entry and owner-independent operations advisor.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container about-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About Les Xu</p>
        <h1>Operator first. Adviser second. That order matters.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Les brings together SME banking, credit analysis, business broking, law and finance training, wholesale operations, hospitality ownership, Vietnam-focused sourcing, and AI-enabled workflow work.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="media-frame">
        <img src="/images/post-08-factory-land-decisions-integrated.png" alt="Vietnam factory and property diligence visual" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container timeline">
      <article>
        <span>Banking</span>
        <h2>Credit and SME risk judgment</h2>
        <p>Commercial lending, client relationships, credit review, branch performance, compliance, and business development built the base for practical risk thinking.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Broking</span>
        <h2>Business-sale and negotiation lens</h2>
        <p>Business broking sharpened the questions around value, buyer concerns, vendor readiness, transaction confidence, and how deals actually move.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Owner-operator</span>
        <h2>Wholesale and hospitality reality</h2>
        <p>Fresh and Chilled and KIN Cafe and Wine Bar added lived operating experience: suppliers, staff, service, leases, local marketing, costs, customers, and daily execution.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Vietnam advisory</span>
        <h2>Market entry and owner-independent systems</h2>
        <p>Today the work focuses on helping foreign founders and SME owners evaluate Vietnam and build calmer operating systems before complexity compounds.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark-band">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What Les is not selling</p>
        <h2>No shortcut story. No easy-money pitch.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lead">
        Vietnam can be a serious opportunity, but serious opportunity needs sequencing, confirmation, partner discipline, capital control, and operating rhythm. That is the lane.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand title="Bring the project before the momentum gets expensive." text="A Reality Check gives you a practical decision sequence before leases, partners, capital, and setup work start moving." />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: 104px 0 72px;
  }

  .about-grid,
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.92fr;
    gap: 52px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .timeline {
    display: grid;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  .timeline article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 180px 0.9fr 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 28px;
  }

  .timeline span {
    color: var(--red);
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", Consolas, monospace;
    font-weight: 900;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .timeline h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.8rem);
  }

  .timeline p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--steel);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-grid,
    .split,
    .timeline article {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
